<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Animating left, top, width, or height forces the browser to redo layout and paint on every frame, and it stutters when the main thread is busy. Animating transform or opacity can skip straight to compositing, and keeps running smoothly.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Wherever the visual result allows it, express slides as translate, resizes as scale, and fades as opacity — same visual outcome, a fraction of the rendering-pipeline cost.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Compositor-only animations run on a thread independent of the main thread, so they keep progressing even while JavaScript is busy — that independence, not just raw speed, is why they stay smooth under real-world load where layout-property animations visibly drop frames.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
